A||N||8||turbo86se||Found an 85GT! ||||5||
Z||000000||turbo86se||10-16-2000||02:48 PM||||Since it is so nice out, instead of golfing I decided to take the turbo SE out for a spin. While I'm sitting at a red light, to my left I notice a Fiero in a used car lot. I make a quick U-turn and pull into the lot. The first thing I notice is the dual exhaust and rounded rear bumper. I thought it was an 86SE V6, then I noticed the GT sailpanels! Cool, a white 85GT!<BR>From the driver's side it looked decent, not taken care of, a flat rear bald tire, expired tags. Then I walk around to the passenger side, uh oh, damage!<BR>This Fiero's been sideswiped, front right fender damaged (not bad), door is in real bad shape, mirror's gone, and a huge gash in the rear notchback panel above the wheel. You could pull the small panel behind the door out, and see down to the ground. The ground FX were in good shape. The interior is trashed, driver's seat ripped bad, very dirty. <BR>156,000 miles, 4-spd, tan interior. Tape with EQ. Didn't look at the engine. <P>I go inside to talk to the salesperson, and find out they're waiting on the title to sell it, since it was repo'd.<BR>They have no idea if it runs or not. I told them I'd buy it "as is."<BR>Gave them my number, and they said they'll get back to me.<P>How much would you pay for this car? Assuming the engine runs? I've got parts to fix it, power doors from a 84SE, fenders... How much if it doesn't run?<BR>Thanks!!!<BR>-joel<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||RobertVol||10-16-2000||03:31 PM||||Because of the damage I personally wouldnt pay more than 700.00 dollars for it. With the mileage and the damage. Because if you look hard enough you probably could find a litter better GT for 1500.00 so subtract the damage and mileage and thats were I get that. BUT just a " IMHO"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Some people may find more value in it. I wouldnt though. <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT 55k  <BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/582bead0.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||10-16-2000||03:32 PM||||Uh that would be Little better ,,not litter. Phew ! Long day ! ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tigger||10-16-2000||03:47 PM||||Sounds like a lot of work and lots of miles already on it.  Having the body panels to replace them with is a plus, but consider the suspension could be shot, did you check for rust in the trunk?<P>I'd see if he'd take $500 for it. <P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||turbo86se||10-16-2000||05:04 PM||||HOLY COW!!!!<BR>I just got off the phone with the guy at the lot, he's got the title, and wants to get a "couple hundred bucks" for it. I offered $200 and he said yes!!  YIPPEEE!<BR>Now tomorrow after school my mechanic and I are going to go check it out to see if anything's wrong with the engine.<BR>I'll keep ya'll posted!!!||||reg||10
Z||000005||2xsess||10-17-2000||05:23 PM||||Cool deal!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||10-18-2000||01:35 PM||||Yesterday my mechanic and I went over there to check out the car. The clutch felt good, no leaks under the car, headlights worked, no damage to frame, passenger door did open and shut securely. Even though the battery had juice, the power latch wouldn't work. My mechanic took the switch cover off and did something, but it wouldn't open. The dealer doesn't have the keys! My mechanic swears the car will run. I haven't decided if I'm going to buy it, but I probably will tomorrow.....||||reg||10
Z||000007||2xsess||10-18-2000||01:44 PM||||If you don't buy it for $200 I'll come up and get it.<P><BR>Keep us posted.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000008||turbo86se||10-19-2000||07:22 PM||||well, I went by today with cash in hand ready to buy the car. The nice lady behind the desk told me that the two owners of the shop decided they were going to fix it and put it out on their lot. You should have seen the mechanic's face!!  He did not look thrilled! LOL<BR>I noticed the car had been moved, they said they had keys made to start it. <P>I'll take this as a sign that I shouldn't buy the car. My backyard needs sod, need a new 3-wood, the 86SE needs a little more pampering.....<BR> <BR>Thanks for looking guys and gals!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
